{
  "claim": "On a plan's page, a link to a flow or a flow's step opens a copy of the flow in a modal, whole, with the step lit and in view, its row left closed and the page where it was. The close button, a click outside and, with real input in Chrome, Esc close it and give the focus back to the link. Only the flow scrolls while it is open. A tip and Comment work in the copy, and a link out of the modal leaves it, with Back returning to the link that opened it. A row's line still opens and closes it in place, and links no name. Seen in Chrome and in the Mac's WebKit. Safari itself has not run it: its remote automation is off. WebKit's page was hidden at this capture (the screen was off), so its scrolls were not smooth, and it has not had a real Esc, wheel or click.",
  "source": "Google Chrome 156 headless, and WebKit 21624 in a WKWebView on macOS 26.5, where Safari 26.5.2 is installed",
